WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.120
If you take medication for diabetes, including insulin or oral medications like

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.720
Metformin,

3
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.680
the day before your procedure requires some extra attention.

4
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.720
Because you'll be on a clear liquid diet today, your usual medication routine

5
00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:13.280
may need to be

6
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:18.200
adjusted to avoid low blood sugar. If you haven't been already instructed,

7
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.040
please contact your

8
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.470
doctor's office or your prescribing physician for specific guidance on what to

9
00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:24.800
take, what to hold,

10
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:30.440
and when. Do not adjust your insulin or diabetes medications on your own. If

11
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.520
you experience any

12
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:36.160
symptoms of low blood sugar, like shakiness, sweating, or confusion, treat it

13
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:36.960
promptly and

14
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.560
contact them right away.
